          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SOME APPLICATIONS OF TRIGONOMETRY"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.862,
            0.104,
            0.898,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "141"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.161,
            0.141,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.146,
            0.555,
            0.189
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{3}{AD}  or   AD = 3\\sqrt{3}  m"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.198,
            0.642,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, in right "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " PBD, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathbf { B } = 4 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . So, BD = PD = 3 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.233,
            0.158,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.325,
            0.227,
            0.779,
            0.252
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "AB = BD + AD = 3 + 3\\sqrt{3} = 3\\left(1 + \\sqrt{3}\\right) m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.267,
            0.581,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the width of the river is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\left( { \\sqrt { 3 } } + 1 \\right)   \\mathrm { m }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.327,
            0.589,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "EXERCISE 9.1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.357,
            0.595,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A circus artist is climbing a 20 m long rope, which is tightly stretched and tied from the top of a vertical pole to the ground. Find the height of the pole, if the angle made by the rope with the ground level is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (see Fig. 9.11)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.622,
            0.356,
            0.883,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.622,
                0.356,
                0.883,
                0.481
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.452,
            0.595,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A tree breaks due to storm and the broken part bends so that the top of the tree touches the ground making an angle "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with it. The distance between the foot of the tree to the point where the top touches the ground is 8 m. Find the height of the tree."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.705,
            0.485,
            0.802,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 9.11"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.562,
            0.902,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A contractor plans to install two slides for the children to play in a park. For the children below the age of 5 years, she prefers to have a slide whose top is at a height of 1.5 m, and is inclined at an angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to the ground, whereas for elder children, she wants to have a steep slide at a height of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3   \\mathrm { m } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and inclined at an angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to the ground. What should be the length of the slide in each case?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.655,
            0.9,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The angle of elevation of the top of a tower from a point on the ground, which is 30 m away from the foot of the tower, is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the height of the tower."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.696,
            0.902,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A kite is flying at a height of 60 m above the ground. The string attached to the kite is temporarily tied to a point on the ground. The inclination of the string with the ground is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the length of the string, assuming that there is no slack in the string."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.755,
            0.902,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A 1.5 m tall boy is standing at some distance from a 30 m tall building. The angle of elevation from his eyes to the top of the building increases from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as he walks towards the building. Find the distance he walked towards the building."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.813,
            0.902,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " From a point on the ground, the angles of elevation of the bottom and the top of a transmission tower fixed at the top of a 20 m high building are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " respectively. Find the height of the tower."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
